Z||000018||loafer87gt||03-13-2001||09:14 AM||||If you want to get into a sunroof equipped fiero all you have to do is hit the 2 bolts area around the latch of your sunroof with the palm of your hand, and whoila, open sesame! ||||reg||1
Z||000019||Cliff Pennock||03-13-2001||11:28 AM||||The reason you couldn't find the original thread is because I deleted it. If you locked your keys in your car, call a locksmith or tiple-A, they'll open your car in a minute. If you need to get into your car badly, because (as was given as an example) you locked your baby inside, well, maybe it's just me but I wouldn't give a rat's ass about trying not to damage my car.<P>And if you need to know "just in case", ask for a reply by email and print out the reply so you'll never forget, because this thread <B>will</B> also disappear in time.<P>If you are really worried you'll lock yourself out of your car one day, carry around a spare key - I do.||||reg||1
Z||000020||Formula88||03-13-2001||12:33 PM||||Just a note for emergency access to your car if you've locked your keys in it (i.e. baby's in car, pet, etc).  Most Police officers carry tools to break into cars and will help you, but only if it's an emergency.  Otherwise you'll have to call a locksmith.||||reg||4
