Z||000025||Cliff Pennock||03-13-2001||08:39 PM||||No disrespect taken, but let me explain why this bothers me. I live downtown a fairly big city. My previous car has been broken into about 12 times in less than 3 months until it was stolen. They leave my Fiero alone because since it's a pretty unique car here in Holland, they (thieves, junks, etc.) have no idea what kind of person drives it. But let me tell you, if they happen to come across a post on a public forum that explains to them how to unlock and hotwire it, my car will be gone the very next day. I just want to get that message across before I delete this thread.||||reg||1
